,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2024-10-30T07:27:12Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T15:12:48Z","closed_at":"2025-04-17T11:27:38Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.0.4\n\n### System information\n\nmacos 14.4 (23E214) godot 4.0.4\n\n### Issue description\n\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7c07c362-2d1a-43d7-869b-13395c4a0d94)\r\n\r\nSet the ior property of Threejs material and change the refractive index of transparent material. The effect is as follows:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/34d3c513-2def-4c6d-96ef-e678c553e342)\r\n\r\nHowever, in Godot's StandMaterial3D, after setting Refraction, regardless of the scale value, the previously transparent material becomes opaque, and the objects that are blocked behind do not refract on the sphere, as shown in the following figure:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2f64af12-0cab-46ce-a040-ac8c79477986)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4e98a3e-f695-48d4-8391-5792e45fc701)\r\n\r\nReferring to the refraction property of StandardMaterial3D, the godot shader script code written is as follows：\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0d0e590c-89cf-4ccd-a46f-a9adba30335b)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2fbef465-9800-45ac-b07f-871ef924be4c)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9be8439c-adfc-4937-95f6-7d2e7d25f2a9)\r\n\r\nThe effect shown above is very different from IOR. Do you have a plan to adapt to IOR, or do you have any good suggestions to solve this problem?\r\n\r\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnone\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Test0520.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17567659/Test0520.zip)\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98663/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98663/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}